#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0353 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. Both rows are baseline records that would read as 'unequal' on a naive comparison - row 1 has a blank B1IND, row 2 a blank A1IND. The authored `not empty(ByIND)` / `not empty(AyIND)` conjuncts keep the rule silent. This pins the authored non-emptiness gate, which the machine derivation does NOT supply for wildcard names: NonEmptyGuardInliner.isPrimaryColumn excludes any name containing `*`, `{` or a lowercase letter, so the authored guards are load-bearing and must not be read as duplicated guards."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ABLFL   type=Char
col A1IND   type=Char
col B1IND   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | Y | NORMAL |
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALT | Y |  | HIGH
